        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-08T13:08:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ouch. This will send the capabilities to ConnectivityService via the NetworkAgent, which incurs a loop around the ConnectivityService handler thread and, I think, a delay inside AsyncChannel. This means that the capability change will be delayed.\n\nI don\u0027t think this is a problem if we get here via the app calling setUnderlyingNetworks, because that call is coming from another process and so doesn\u0027t have a strong ordering relationship with ConnectivityService events.\n\nHowever, I think it is a problem if we get here via an internal CS event such as a VPN connecting or a capability change in one of the VPN\u0027s underlying networks. In that case, even if we call this method on the handler thread, its effects will be delayed. For example it looks like the following could happen:\n\n1. Device switches from wifi to cell with a VPN up.\n2. CS, updates VPN\u0027s underlying network based on new default, calls updateAllVpnsCapabilities, sends CONNECTIVITY_ACTION broadcast. New metered capabilities sent to network agent.\n3. App receives CONNECTIVITY_ACTION broadcast and immediately calls isActiveNetworkMetered.\n4. isActiveNetworkMetered returns false because new metered capabilities have not made it to CS yet.\n5. App proceeds to do large transfer on cell data.\n\nOr, the opposite can happen: when switching from cell to wifi, an app immediately calls isActiveNetworkMetered, gets true, and doesn\u0027t do what it\u0027s supposed to do on unmetered networks (e.g., download files).\n\nI don\u0027t see a simple solution to this problem other than having updateAllVpnsCapabilities directly call Vpn#updateCapabilities inline on the ConnectivityService handler thread. That\u0027s not a trivial change.\n\nI don\u0027t know what that means for this CL. Perhaps we should get it in regardless since I think it\u0027s mostly a step in the right direction.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 293,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 293,
        "endChar": 49
      },
